The base case corrects for overly high photooxidation of DOCr that causes a negative bias in the deep ocean.

Deep ocean O2 inventory is still bad, but we don't compute DOCr to O2 quotients in the deep ocean. 

The optimized parameter changes from out of the box CESM2.1.3 include DOMr_reminR_photo= 80 yr (was 18 yrs), 
parm_scalelen_vals = 0.8, 2.8, 3.6, 3.8 (was 1, 3.3, 4.2, 4.4), 
kappa_isop*2.5, G1850NYR, ladjust_bury_coeff=true. 

changes made include:

marbl_settings_mod.F90: 
  DOMr_reminR_photo = (c1/(365.0_r8*80.0_r8)) * dps       ! additional remin from photochemistry, 1/80yrs over top 10m

user_nl_pop
  modified FeSedflux inputs, dust flux inputs, iron flux inputs, feventflux inputs, and river dfe flux scale factor

user_nl_marbl
  ladjust_bury_coeff = .true.
  parm_scalelen_vals = 0.8, 2.8, 3.6, 3.8

hmix_gm.F90
  Kappa_isop*2.5

vmix_kpp_modified.F90
  Bckgrnd_vdc (regional enhancements Sea of Japan, Bering Sea, Kuril region)

G1850NYR
  compset: 1850_DATM%NYF_SLND_CICE_POP2%ECO_DROF%NYF_SGLC_SWAV

box_atm_co2
  ./xmlchange --file env_run.xml --id OCN_CO2_TYPE --val box_atm_co2




